@kommander not too sure to understand your suggestion.  Are you suggesting this should be a custom plugin (for myself) rather than a change to the actual default TUI ?

Similarly to an PR on Github, I think we should have a way to see global additions/deletion at a glance? 

<img width="220" height="95" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a1758663-428a-4505-8625-f6f000d2678a" />

> Is there any workaround for this? I can no longer use my Kimi coding plan.

Try add this to opencode config
```
"kimi-for-coding": {
      "models": {
        "k2p6":             { "headers": { "User-Agent": "KimiCLI/1.5" } },
        "k2p5":             { "headers": { "User-Agent": "KimiCLI/1.5" } },
        "kimi-k2-thinking": { "headers": { "User-Agent": "KimiCLI/1.5" } }
      }
    },
```

@twhittock oh I think this is a problem with how you are hitting the endpoint. You need to pass the same `directory` param on all HTTP requests so it would be `/session/<session_id>/prompt_async?directory=<projectdir>`. Can you try that and see if that works?

If you use the SDK you can provide the project directly once when creating the client and then it automatically does that

I agree this is confusing, in the next iteration of our APIs we are fixing this so can you create a session in whatever context and you won't need to pass anything in future calls

There is no "go binary" if u are using a custom model u can define it like so:
```
"provider": {
    "my-provider": {
      "models": {
        "my-model": {
          "modalities": {
            "input": ["text", "image", "pdf"],
            "output": ["text"],
          },
        },
      },
    },
  },
```
